Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(knowledge): unblock bearer-agent reads (port
 operator #1461 + extend to graph/domains) (#49)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Browse routes 403'd every bearer-token request even though getSessionUser is
bearer-first and the knowledge.list contract already declares
KNOWLEDGE_READ_REQUIRES_PRINCIPAL. Agents could WRITE contributions but never
READ the plane they wrote to.

Operator fixed this in #1461 for list + [id]; node-template never got the port,
and operator never finished domains (still cookie-only) or graph (node-only feature).

This removes the bearer-403 guard on all four read routes:
- GET /knowledge (list)        — mirrors operator #1461
- GET /knowledge/[id]          — mirrors operator #1461
- GET /knowledge/graph         — node-only; agents can now pull citation links
- GET /knowledge/domains (list) — extends past operator

Invariant KNOWLEDGE_BROWSE_VIA_HTTP_REQUIRES_SESSION -> KNOWLEDGE_READ_REQUIRES_PRINCIPAL
(DOMAIN_LIST_COOKIE_ONLY -> DOMAIN_LIST_REQUIRES_PRINCIPAL). Human-UI fetchers
stay cookie-only by construction. Adds a contract test proving bearer agents
get 200 (not 403) on all four routes incl. graph edge link-pulling.

Full-text search remains a gap (port exposes only list/get, no query).
